  update --all discards already-applied updates on first failure.

  The loop aborts and returns nil, err as soon as one skill fails,
  silently losing the fact that prior skills in the batch were already
  updated on disk. Callers get no partial results and no indication of what
  succeeded.

  Consider collecting per-skill results (with a failure status/error) and
  continuing the loop, returning the full batch alongside an aggregate error
  (or per-item error info) so callers can see what actually happened.





