  Missing internal/skills.VerifyContent scan on load.

  ReadInstalledSkill is the shared path used by both FindInstalledSkill
  and ListInstalledSkills to decode marketplace-installed skill content,
  but it never calls skills.VerifyContent. Marketplace-installed skills
  aren't bundled/embedded, so per the skill-scanning guideline this read
  path should scan content on every load and block critical findings
  (logging warnings/info otherwise).





  🛡️ Suggested fix sketch

   func ReadInstalledSkill(skillDir string) (InstalledSkill, error) {
   	provenance, err := skills.ReadSidecar(skillDir)
   	if err != nil {
   		return InstalledSkill{}, err
   	}
   	if provenance == nil {
   		return InstalledSkill{}, classifiedf(ErrNotMarketplace, "missing provenance for %q", skillDir)
   	}
   
   	skillFile, err := registrypkg.PathWithinRoot(skillDir, SkillMarkdownFileName)
   	if err != nil {
   		return InstalledSkill{}, fmt.Errorf("resolve skill file in %q: %w", skillDir, err)
   	}
   
   	parsedSkill, err := skills.ParseSkillFile(skillFile)
   	if err != nil {
   		return InstalledSkill{}, err
   	}
  +
  +	if err := skills.VerifyContent(parsedSkill); err != nil {
  +		return InstalledSkill{}, err
  +	}
   
   	return InstalledSkill{
   		Name:       parsedSkill.Meta.Name,
   		Dir:        parsedSkill.Dir,
   		FilePath:   parsedSkill.FilePath,
   		Provenance: *provenance,
   	}, nil
   }

  Based on learnings (path instructions): internal/skills//*.go: "Scan
  every non-bundled skill with internal/skills.VerifyContent on every
  load; block critical findings, log warnings, and silently log
  informational findings. Bundled embedded skills are exempt."


