  critical [Security & Privacy]
  → ]8;;vscode://file//Users/pedronauck/Dev/compozy/agh/internal/skills/marketplace/paths.go:18internal/skills/marketplace/paths.go:18-58]8;;

  Return the resolved path, not the unresolved absTarget.

  PathInsideRoot validates containment using resolvedTarget (symlinks
  resolved via EvalSymlinks) but returns absTarget (unresolved). Callers
  then perform file I/O against the unresolved path, so any symlink along
  the way is re-traversed at use time — decoupling the validated location
  from the actually-accessed location (TOCTOU / symlink-escape window). Per
  path instructions for this package, containment checks must rely on
  EvalSymlinks-resolved targets; returning the resolved value closes this
  gap.





  🛡️ Proposed fix

   	if relative == ".." || strings.HasPrefix(relative, ".."+string(filepath.Separator)) {
   		return "", registrypkg.ErrPathOutsideRoot
   	}
  -	return absTarget, nil
  +	return resolvedTarget, nil
   }

  Based on path instructions: "Verify resolved filesystem targets remain
  inside approved roots using EvalSymlinks and path-prefix checks"
  (internal/{skills,fileutil,extension,bundles}//*.go).


